  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-13, in chat, on v0.19.0): \"when hovering a \"selection\" in the geometry tab of an operation it should clearly highlight in the viewwport which you are gonna delete for example..\"\n\nWhat happens: the Geometry tab of an operation lists its selections as rows (for example \"Chain Body1 · open · 50.0 mm · 1 of 2\", \"Face Body1 · z=0.00 · 1250 mm2\"), each with a remove button. Hovering a row or its remove button shows nothing in the viewport, so the user cannot tell which edge, chain or face the row stands for before removing it.\n\nExpected: while the pointer is over a selection row (or its remove button), that face, edge, chain or vertex is drawn in the viewport with a strong hover highlight, clearly different from the normal selected style and visible on the shaded and wireframe model in both themes. The highlight goes away when the pointer leaves. The other direction helps too: hovering a selected entity in the viewport marks its row in the list.\n\nThis is hover state: immediate-mode only, not a command and not undoable (Everything Is a Command, \"Ephemeral UI state\"). The UI passes the hovered row to the viewport through the app layer, not by a direct world call from the panel.\n\nRelated: issue 1505 (selected edges are too faint; edge picking is unpredictable). The hover style and the selected style should be chosen together.\n\nDone means: a ui test through the test harness hovers a selection row and asserts the viewport's highlighted entity is that row's entity, and none after the pointer leaves; it holds for face, edge/chain and vertex rows; the highlight style is a named constant covered by the structural test; before and after screenshots in the PR.\n",
